{"id": "EUVD-2026-103572", "enisaUuid": "7ef1774e-fa7b-339c-964a-54586827ffdf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: zynq: fix runtime PM leak on request error path\n\npm_runtime_get_sync() leaves the usage counter incremented even when it\nfails, and zynq_gpio_request() returns the error without dropping it.\n\ngpiolib does not call ->free() when ->request() fails, so zynq_gpio_free(),\nwhich holds the only matching pm_runtime_put(), never runs. The reference\nis leaked and the controller can no longer runtime-suspend, so its clock\nstays enabled.\n\nSwitch to pm_runtime_resume_and_get(), which only increments the usage\ncounter on success.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e380fba02908b809f5bbef371259003cf5887bb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3e9b7f7c9558f8c9592f8f817557bff98707bb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60a76cdd92e25f576dc58d756a565760dde1f7a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25c08be2a5e7715f19a6e02bbe9b0e5f01c77aac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e05f1c614a57a5d4c364dd12e20c6fd012f9d3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58a417a19d80141fff3abe6004e2e47285506e73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e20dabffbcd7b222d8e7bb85a7d8e8325df7699", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9438ab5328a177c9c0e5df87eb92a7162841e98"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xv89-vpfw-p3mv", "CVE-2026-98527"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "004b617c-3d66-35bb-868d-b30ec0470d27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3242ba117e9bd29eb748afd6f6fbfbd6dd7cfe52 <e380fba02908b809f5bbef371259003cf5887bb4"}, {"id": "1a32b124-9b12-3994-9365-bfd95c79e9aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "2a3f8603-cf70-3fe4-ac32-f6d31b9a158a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "